@0    = ~Free! I am free at last! I thank you, my saviors, for freeing me from being controlled by this nabassu fledgling. His death gaze hit me just as my friend and I entered these halls, and I have been bound to serve him ever since.~
@1    = ~Klaus made it outside, but... I don't think he is well, considering you must have the scroll to enter the dungeons...?~
@2    = ~He is alive, in case you are worried about that.~
@3    = ~Last time I saw him, he was in Balduran's Seatower, conjuring rabbits. *Lots* of rabbits.~
@4    = ~Oh, he gave it to me of his own free will. At least I would call it that.~
@5    = ~What of it?~
@6    = ~So you are the one that crazy mage was talking about.~
@7    = ~Oh, you mean that crazy mage was talking about saving *you*? I thought he was talking about our "host" Alguine!~
@8    = ~Oh, I wasn't implying anything!~
@9    = ~He did?~
@10   = ~Erm, rabbits...?~
@11   = ~Just that I thought he would... well, search for a way to help me, is all.~
@12   = ~Oh, he did. Believe me, he did.~
@13   = ~Well—here we are! No?~
@14   = ~He wasn't really able to, but I think he tried.~
@15   = ~Why don't you go and find out yourself?~
@16   = ~Ah! Oh! I see!~
@17   = ~I need to find him and see how he fares. The poor man, he must be really desperate... Thank you, my saviors. I have nothing on me that could be of use to you, but next time we meet, I'll have something ready to give you!~
@18   = ~Crazy mage? Are you talking about Klaus, by any chance?~
@19   = ~I think that was his name, yes. He was searching for someone strong enough to save "him". So I guess he was referring to you?~
@20   = ~Rats! There are rats everywhere! I swear I saw rats running around above. This is so filthy!~
@21   = ~Don't open that door! He's doing it again. That man is *crazy*!~
@22   = ~I need to conjure the right ones. The right ones will free him! The right ones will kill the beast. The right ones...~
@23   = ~Not the right one! Never the right one... I... I will never save him... Never...~
@24   = ~Oh no, Mr. Klaus! Ye remember what was said, don't ye? Now I need t' kick ye out o' th' inn... I'm very sorry, ye need t' believe me!~
@25   = ~Come o', grab yer things—leave th' rabbits, I'll go chasing them in a moment—and follow me, please...~
@26   = ~Now I can call the right ones! Do you want to see?~
@27   = ~Ah, here you are. What is it you want to show me?~
@28   = ~What do you mean, you can conjure brown rabbits now?~
@29   = ~Leave me be. I just chased all your stupid rabbits through the tavern's aisles, and I really don't want to see any more.~
@30   = ~Don't you dare conjure another rabbit in my presence.~
@31   = ~But... it's the right ones now! It has to be. I need to show someone, or I won't be sure!~
@32   = ~Can I show you now?~
@33   = ~Now I have time, yes.~
@34   = ~*sigh* Fine, then show me.~
@35   = ~No.~
@36   = ~No, the color is irrelevant.~
@37   = ~It's the teeth! Look at the teeth!~
@38   = ~Need to test them... the right ones!~
@39   = ~No! NO!! Dead! It is dead... It is not strong enough... Never strong enough...~
@40   = ~What in the names of the gods was that?~
@41   = ~A vampiric rabbit? Really?~
@42   = ~Why don't we see whether you are strong enough, you idiot!~
@43   = ~But *you* are! You are strong enough! Take this and go inside. Destiny wants you to! Destiny! Yes! And save him... Please save him... He's in the ruins, the old ruins in the Wood of Sharp Teeth... he's trapped!~
@44   = ~It will be an honor to help your friend.~
@45   = ~Er, what?~
@46   = ~We are talking about a person, yes? Not a rabbit? And especially not that last type, hmm?~
@47   = ~A dungeon to explore? Sure, why not.~
@48   = ~Stop tucking filthy scrolls into my robe!~
@49   = ~Please... someone has to save him...~
@50   = ~Now *what* in Selûne's name was that? We have enough trouble and work fighting off the abominations that disgrace our goddess's realms! We do *not* need new undead creations on top of it!~
@51   = ~It was a vampiric rabbit, I wager.~
@52   = ~Oh, that's rich. Now where were you people when I actually *fought* that undead rabbit?~
@53   = ~We came here as fast as we could. You did make enough noise, mind.~
@54   = ~Well then, what do we do with this stupid fool?!~
@55   = ~This man is very troubled, priestess of Selûne. We monks of Ilmater will take him in and give him shelter, until his racing mind calms down again.~
@56   = ~Pfft, suit yourselves. But I guarantee you we will *not* be able to hear your screams if that madman continues to conjure vampiric rabbits inside the monastery. *snort*~
@57   = ~Thank you so much for helping us!~
@58   = ~Save him... need to find a way, a way...~
@59   = ~Klaus, I am truly sorry, but I did not free Ulf.~
@60   = ~Whoops, I knew there was *something* I was supposed to do in that dungeon.~
@61   = ~You... you made it!~
@62   = ~Nooo!... No! Ulf...~
@63   = ~Someone needs to save him...~
@64   = ~Oh! Oh, look who is here, Klaus! It's the adventurers who saved me! Welcome! Welcome, my friends.~
@65   = ~I... I thank you for saving my friend.~
@66   = ~I said I would have a reward ready when next we meet. Let me get it quickly.~
@67   = ~Don't worry about a reward.~
@68   = ~It's good to see you all well.~
@69   = ~It's about time!~
@70   = ~What? Oh, no, no, no.~
@71   = ~You deserve a reward, and we are more than willing to give you one for what you've done.~
@72   = ~What you did for us was generous, to say the least. Here, I hope this will be of use to you.~
@73   = ~All I can say is that it's a bad idea to go dungeon crawling if you are only a group of two mages. A very bad idea.~
@74   = ~I mean... er, it was for *us*, that is. Heh.~
@75   = ~I do not mean to sound ungrateful, but Klaus is in very bad condition and needs to rest again soon.~
@76   = ~Do you have any more questions?~
@77   = ~Can you tell me something about this dungeon?~
@78   = ~All right, I can't keep quiet anymore. WHY RABBITS?~
@79   = ~No more questions. I hope you'll be fine.~
@80   = ~I'll leave you two alone, then.~
@81   = ~The Labyrinth of Future Memories, yes. We read about it in a very old tome and discovered Almiran's scroll soon afterward. We don't know too much about it, though; there is little to find—mainly descriptions of people who found the entrance and went into it, at least from those who came out sane, as it can go quite differently, too. The Thayan mage Almiran was the first to find a direct entrance and to stabilize it with his scroll. We don't know what became of him.~
@82   = ~Apparently, only the one given the scroll will see "future memories" of his life. We didn't know this when we acquired the scroll. Klaus was the chosen one in our case... I just went along and watched him suffer...~
@83   = ~Didn't... mean to. Was aiming for bigger... but was also scared to really call anything else.~
@84   = ~Poor Klaus has had the attention span of a toddler since the fight with the nabassu. I guess the dungeon added to it. As I already said, we appreciate your help with everything.~
@85   = ~Our sincere thanks will accompany you, friend. We are very sorry you were in so much trouble because of us.~
@86   = ~Really sorry... didn't know how else to help Ulf...~
@87   = ~Klaus, don't overstrain yourself. Come, sit down for a moment.~
@88   = ~Not right. You are the one who was turned into a ghast for all these months... Should take care of you, not the other way around...~
@89   = ~Nonsense. I'm as good as new. You are the one worrying and searching all the time, weakened by that dungeon. Here, take this blanket... Do you want something to drink? I could ask the cook for one of her fine broths...~
@90   = ~You will always be welcome here, friend.~
